            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Did not go through in detail, but looks good to me.\n\nPackageParser can be rebased on top of this with minimal changes\n\n```\ndiff --git a/bindings/cpp/firmware_update.cpp b/bindings/cpp/firmware_update.cpp\nindex 613df98..e477742 100644\n--- a/bindings/cpp/firmware_update.cpp\n+++ b/bindings/cpp/firmware_update.cpp\n@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@ pldm::fw_update::PackageParser::parse(\n {\n        const size_t pkgSize = pkg.size();\n \n-       struct pldm_package_iter packageItr = {};\n+       struct pldm_package packageItr = {};\n        std::vector<FirmwareDeviceIDRecord> fwDeviceIDRecords = {};\n        pldm_package_header_information_pad hdr = {};\n        int rc;\n```\n\nand all it's tests still pass."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Nice."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the feedback."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/firmware_update.h",
                    "line": 2485,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I wonder if we need this requirement since it's an out parameter.\n\nZero initializing it would cause runtime overhead but simplify the API for the caller."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/firmware_update.h",
                    "line": 2485,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "The purpose of this statement is to require the user to not pass in partial state from a previous parsing effort, so the implementation can assume it's starting from the expected (initial) state."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/firmware_update.h",
                    "line": 2614,
